I come back home in the evening.
Today is Saturday, so I am making a special dinner.
Asha is coming to my house for dinner tonight.
I go into the kitchen and wash my hands.
I want to make my favourite Mexican dish.
But today, I am trying something new.
I take out the Indian spices from the cupboard.
I bought these spices from the market just yesterday.
First, I heat some oil in a pan.
Then I put onions, tomatoes, and garlic in it.
I add cumin, turmeric, and coriander powder to the vegetables.
I also add some Mexican chili powder to it.
I mix everything well and cook it slowly.
A wonderful, spicy smell fills my kitchen.
This smell reminds me of my home in Mexico.
But the Indian spices make it feel completely different.
I taste the food with a spoon.
It is perfectly spicy and very delicious!
Now I am just waiting for Asha.
